e size conversions in both binary and SI modes. zero bytes returns \"0\"; boundary values at each unit threshold; output uses at most one decimal place. I'm organizing the test structure with separate test files for each module, using table-driven tests with subtests to match the existing patterns in the codebase. For color tests, I'll force color mode on during testing and clean up afterward to avoid TTY dependencies.\n\nNow I'm reviewing the acceptance criteria: all exported functions need test coverage, edge cases like empty slices and multi-byte UTF-8 need handling, and both the test suite and linter checks need to pass cleanly. The plan stays within the constraints—three files, three requirements, four acceptance criteria—and targets around 200-250 lines of production code anchored to the specific PRD requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":53394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10075,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cbf0ca2-d776-4162-8b14-b0e7060738a2","uuid":"ebaef867-7cd2-4129-82cb-000000000000"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JUpyjCQZ62bkAAzcbjU9Fh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. This project derives specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go binaries), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets, excluded from generation).\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists for `pkg/format/` (align.go, color.go, size.go), `pkg/sys/` (stat.go, stat_darwin.go, stat_linux.go, terminal.go), and `pkg/testutils/` (difftest.go, runner.go, plus tests). No `cmd/` code exists on the working branch. `pkg/testutils/` has tests; `pkg/format/` and `pkg/sys/` do not.\n\n**Current release (00.0)**: Four use cases — uc001-magefiles (cmd/version), uc002-format, uc003-sys, uc004-testutils. The latter three have implementation code already present. pkg/format and pkg/sys lack unit tests.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 use cases uc002-format, uc003-sys, and uc004-testutils have implementation code in source_code. uc004-testutils also has tests. The gaps are:\n1. **pkg/format tests** — implementation exists, no tests (uc002)\n2. **pkg/sys tests** — implementation exists, no tests (uc003)\n3. **cmd/version** — neither implementation nor tests exist (uc001)\n\nPer P5 (libraries before CLI) and P8 (implementation before tests, but libraries before consumers), tests for existing shared packages take priority over new CLI code. Between pkg/format and pkg/sys, alphabetical ordering (P8 tiebreaker) selects pkg/format first. The source code comments provide concrete PRD requirement anchors: prd003-format R1 (alignment), R2 (color), R3 (size).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/format: Unit tests for alignment, color, and size (prd003-format R1, R2, R3)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd003-format.yaml (PRD with requirements R1, R2, R3)\n      - pkg/format/align.go (column alignment implementation to test)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (ANSI color implementation to test)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (human-readable size implementation to test)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/align_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for PadRight, PadLeft, Columns, displayWidth, columnWidths, totalWidth\n      - path: pkg/format/color_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled\n      - path: pkg/format/size_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Tests for HumanSize in binary and SI modes\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test column alignment functions per prd003-format R1: PadRight and PadLeft with widths shorter than, equal to, and exceeding the input; displayWidth for ASCII and multi-byte UTF-8 strings; Columns with varying entry counts and terminal widths including single entry, entries exceeding terminal width, and empty input; columnWidths and totalWidth for correct column-width computation with two-space separators\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test ANSI color functions per prd003-format R2: FileTypeColor returns correct escape sequences for each file type (directory, symlink, executable, block device, char device, socket, pipe, regular) and permission-based overrides (setuid, setgid, sticky, other-writable, sticky+other-writable); Reset returns reset sequence when color is enabled and empty string when disabled; SetColorEnabled and ResetColorEnabled toggle forced color mode\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test human-readable size formatting per prd003-format R3: HumanSize with binary mode (base 1024, K/M/G/T/P/E suffixes) and SI mode (base 1000, kB/MB/GB/TB suffixes); zero bytes returns \\\"0\\\" in both modes; boundary values at each unit threshold; output uses at most one decimal place\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Test files mirror source files per project convention: align_test.go, color_test.go, size_test.go\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use table-driven tests with t.Run subtests, matching the pattern established in pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go and runner_test.go\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Color tests call SetColorEnabled(true) to force color on without requiring a TTY, and call ResetColorEnabled in cleanup via t.Cleanup to avoid polluting other tests\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/format/... passes with zero failures\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Every exported function in align.go, color.go, and size.go has at least one test case\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Edge cases covered: empty slice for Columns, zero bytes for HumanSize, all os.FileMode type bits for FileTypeColor, multi-byte UTF-8 input for displayWidth\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/format/... passes with no warnings\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":53394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10075,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cbf0ca2-d776-4162-8b14-b0e7060738a2","uuid":"ebaef867-7cd2-4129-82cb-000000000001"}
